body:
issue (blocking): `order!` hides the null from the compiler, it doesn't remove it. For an unknown id this throws and the caller gets a 500.

```suggestion
    if (await db.Orders.FindAsync(id) is not { } order) return Results.NotFound();
    order.Status = "cancelled";
```

I reproduced it: POST /orders/2147483647/cancel answers 500.
